# Copy to .env.local and enter a server-side API key. Never use NEXT_PUBLIC_ for secrets.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.4
OPENAI_TRANSCRIBE_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini-transcribe
# Optional absolute data directory. Default: web/.venture-pass
# VENTURE_DATA_DIR=
# Optional READ-ONLY comparison history. Requires an existing SQL13 store and its
# matching witness/control directory. Also set an absolute VENTURE_DATA_DIR.
# No directory, database, schema migration, AI execution or approval is created.
# The database UUID must match the production/live selection already recorded.
# Restart the local server after changing these settings. Do not use NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# VENTUREPASS_COMPARISON_REVIEW_DATABASE_ID=
# VENTUREPASS_COMPARISON_REVIEW_CONTROL_DIR=
# Explicit comparison execution HTTP/UI assembly (operational activation still separate).
# Separate explicit settings; read-only review settings never enable execution.
# Execution requires OPENAI_API_KEY and an existing SQL13 store with matching witnesses.
# The explicit company reservation-list GET uses these DB/path settings without a key.
# It reads input-file selection metadata only; no execution/settings change or consent.
# Every send still requires its original current approval, reservation and SQL owner.
# A changed key/path/UUID revokes the retained owner; keep it for recovery/cleanup.
# Do not set OPENAI_CUSTOM_HEADERS. No schema migration or paid call occurs on import.
# VENTUREPASS_COMPARISON_EXECUTION_DATABASE_ID=
# VENTUREPASS_COMPARISON_EXECUTION_CONTROL_DIR=
# HTTP open requires an existing server-owned JSON input file alongside the
# configured control directory (outside witness journals): {inputVersion:1,databaseInstanceId,settings:{
# companyId,companyRevision,runId,basis,usagePolicy}}. The run must already be reserved.
# basis/usagePolicy must be reviewed policies accepted by their existing schemas/audits.
# This file is NOT user consent and creates no approval, reservation or pricing evidence.
# HTTP never writes it. The explicit local comparison:prepare-input command can audit
# existing reservations/policies and export a NEW file without a key or provider call.
# It never activates these settings. No key, customer document or input file belongs in Git.
# File/path/content changes revoke NEW sends at the existing final runtime checks;
# original HTTP tickets still allow state/recovery/cleanup. A new open needs a client UUID;
# retries must reuse that UUID and original company revision to recover the same ticket.
# VENTUREPASS_COMPARISON_EXECUTION_INPUT_FILE=
# Optional NEW comparison booking UI: explicit reviewed financial-evidence file,
# a regular file beside the control directory: {policyVersion:1,databaseInstanceId,evidence}.
# evidence must satisfy comparisonFinancialEvidenceSchema with official-reviewed provenance.
# This is separate from the transmission/usage policy file; it is NOT consent.
# No defaults, fabricated pricing, migrations, budget creation or automatic activation.
# Selection IDs come from the UI; model, evidence and budget remain server-owned.
# Changes revoke new reviews/reservations; original recovery/close remain available.
# No key or external call is needed to review/book. Reservation writes require five consents.
# VENTUREPASS_COMPARISON_RESERVATION_POLICY_FILE=
